*   **Lone Pairs:** The two lone pairs are located on the two ends of the molecule. This causes distortion of the molecule from a tetrahedral shape. The two lone pairs repel the F atoms more strongly, pulling them towards the sides, resulting the T-shape.

Therefore, the shape is T-shaped.
