","Here calculation of the magnetic field at the center of a circular coil:

**Formula:**

The magnetic field (B) at the center of a circular coil is given by the following formula:

B = (2πμ₀NI) / (2πR)
B = (μ₀NI) / R

where:

* B is the magnetic field in Tesla (T)

* μ₀ is the permeability of free space (approximately 4π x 10⁻⁷ T⋅m/A)
    *  This is a constant.
* N is the number of turns in the coil (in this case, 100)
* I is the current flowing through the coil (in this case, 1 A)

0.  R is the radius of the coil (in meter, in this case, 0.2 m)

