Work in physics is defined as the work done by a force force on an object over a distance. It is only work if the force is in the direction of the displacement.

**Formula**

The work (W) is calculated as:

W = F * d * cos(θ)

where:
* F is the magnitude of the force (in News)
    * F = 60.0 N
* d is the distance (in meters)
