    *  $d = 6 \times 10^{-8} \text{ m}$
    *  $b'^2 = 1.17$

    $\Delta \sigma_{ur} = \frac{(26 \times 10^9 \text{ N/m}^2) (0.286 \times 10^{-9} \text{ m})}{6 \000000 \times 10^{-8} \text{ m}} \sqrt{1.17}$

    $\Delta \s{}\text{{r}}_{ur} = \frac{7.436 \times 10^9 \text{ N}}{m}^2}{6 \times 10^{-8} \text{ m}} \sqrt{1.17}$

    $\Delta \sigma_{ur} = 1.236 \times 10^{17} \text{ N/m}^2 \sqrt{1.17}$

    $\Delta \sigma_{ur} = 1.236 \times 10^{17} \text{ N/m}^2 \times 1.082$

    $\Delta \s{}\text{{r}}_{ur} \approx 1.33 \times 10^{17} \text{ N/m}^2$

