$V_1 = 4 \text{ L}$
$V_2 = 8 \text{ L}$
The problem states that the process is isothermal, which means the temperature remains constant.
The work is given by:
$$W = -P_1 V_1 \ln\left(\frac{V_2}{V_1}\right)$$
$$W = - (2 \text{ atm}) (4 \text{ L}) \ln\left(\frac{8 \text{ L}}{4 \text{ L}}\right)$$
$$W = - 8 \text{ atm L} \ln(2)$$
Since $1 \text{ atm L} = 1 \text{ L atm} = 0.0984 \text{ L atm}$, we can convert the result to liters-atm:
