*  ΔG is the Gibbs Free Energy
*  R is the gas constant (8.14 J/mol·K)

*  T is the temperature in Kelvin (37°C = 310 K)
*  K is the equilibrium constant

We can calculate K from the change in Gibbs free energy at standard conditions:

K = exp(-ΔG₀/RT)

